> Note that the switch block is the same like the others and case and
> default and very similar to goto labels. You can even do:
> switch (x) {
> int abc;
> { case 5: abc = 7; break; }
> do { case 3: abc = 5; break; } while (0);
> while (1) {
>         printf("%d\n", abc);
> default:
>         abc = 1;
> }
> }
> And check what it will do for x == 3, 5, and others :).

